### 5.1 Upstream performance and final confirmation

Performance has two non-interchangeable roles:

1. During `architecture_optimality_synthesis`, static operation/lock/allocation/
   wake bounds eliminate dominated candidates and controlled construction
   measurements select `X2` only among `X1` ties.
2. During `empirical_performance_acceptance`, hash-recorded release binaries
   confirm the frozen selection after complete correctness.

Moving architecture selection to the second role is a phase-order violation.
Using the first role to accept release correctness is an evidence violation.
The matrix therefore defines distinct typed records: Construction records are
admitted only for multiple `X1` minimizers and cannot prove release acceptance;
Acceptance records bind the frozen universe and release binary and cannot
select or repair topology. Deterministic scenarios bind parameters and runner
source; generated/randomized inputs additionally bind fixture/generator hash
and seed.

If the executable static frontier proves `|X1| = 1`, then for every empirical
objective `J_e`, `argmin J_e over X1 = X1`. The Construction measurement
universe is therefore empty by admission, `X2 = X1`, and fabricating a timing
comparison is a phase violation. This algebra does not discharge the later
fixed-binary Acceptance matrix.

### 5.2 Optimality certificate boundary

The final scoped claim requires all of:

- content-addressed release basis and generated candidate partition;
- coverage of all admissible normal forms modulo external observation;
- feasibility proof per partition and conditional static lower bounds;
- witness static cost equal to those bounds;
- declared workload/environment matrix and noise-gated empirical frontier;
- conditional complexity lower bounds and witness equality;
- production refinement plus static/empirical/complexity cost binding; and
- independent negative canaries for omitted constraints, objective reorder,
  downstream selection and an uncertified optimum.

Without every item, `current_claim` remains `unproved`.
An uncertified result is a release blocker. There is no implicit `best known`
degradation path; changing that disposition requires an explicit user goal
change and a new release-law basis.

## 6. Phase execution rule

For every phase:

1. Read the current rank items and their unique blocker owners.
2. Regenerate the top-down and bottom-up obligation differences.
3. Reproduce and trace all related candidates before selecting one root.
4. Update the executable model, candidate comparison and fixed plan delta.
5. Implement the smallest root correction in reviewable semantic slices.
6. Run static, model, focused and complete affected evidence proportional to
   risk; record exact universe and artifacts.
7. Generate source/authority/task/effect/compatibility and evidence ownership
   checks; remove the invalid state and obsolete route.
8. Emit the actual new rank and prove it strictly decreased, or record the new
   legal counterexample that justifiably reopens the basis.
9. Re-derive the canonical goal, stable `AGENTS.md` method and entire remaining
   DAG, then apply the whole-system checkpoint: authority count, transition
   totality, conservation, fault/wait/publication graphs, compatibility,
   concurrency, cost, risk transfer and snowball complexity.
10. Freeze a recoverable local checkpoint and continue to the next ready phase.

No phase may disappear, reorder or close from prose. A new semantic case,
authority, failure domain, compatibility decision or concurrency topology first
changes the model and machine plan. Additive oracle strength is evidence-only
only when it changes no product or release law.

## 7. Anti-recurrence canaries

| Prior failure class | Mechanical rejection condition |
|---|---|
| Closed-world review missed requirements | Either independently generated basis difference is nonempty. |
| Prose finding vanished from TODOs | Any open prose ID has zero or multiple construction-rank/blocker owners. |
| Diagnostic tool became policy authority | A Rust API delta tool result substitutes for the total compatibility decision or landing evidence. |
| Performance appeared only downstream | Architecture-selection phase is not upstream of semantic closure and evidence freeze. |
| Construction timing became release evidence | A Construction record is referenced by Acceptance or lacks the X1 candidate partition; an Acceptance record lacks the frozen universe/release binary or selects topology. |
| Schedule pressure weakened the final goal | The release gate admits an uncertified or implicit `best known` disposition without an explicit user goal change. |
| Apparent independence removed a real DAG edge | A phase/family is parallelized while its generated owner/candidate-path intersection is nonempty. |
| Symbolic convergence hid no progress | Current status omits named rank values or a step fails to decrease rank. |
| Mutation kept extending the release | A nonterminal candidate, timeout or new semantic family survives universe freeze. |
| Cleanup invalidated final evidence | Constructive simplification is ordered after mutation/correctness. |
| Tests changed release semantics silently | A model/release-law test change is classified evidence-only. |
| Plan history resurrected stale work | More than one current roadmap/status owner or a historical directive issues work. |
| Complexity accumulated as insurance | A state/lock/task/queue/proof mechanism lacks a unique fact and deletion counterexample. |
| Local success became a global claim | Objective order, coverage, lower bound, witness or negative certificate is absent. |
| Ignored method drifted across devices | Current checkpoint omits the verified SHA-256 of root `AGENTS.md`. |

